# Throwaway harnesses review lenses write while checking a fix. They have Bash
# access on purpose — one examined 432,954 graph swaps to verify an objective — but
# nothing tells an agent to clean up, and a probe left under app/test or lib/test
# gets picked up by vitest, runs for 90 s, times out, and reads as a FAILING test
# on the next run. Give them somewhere that is neither a test glob nor tracked.
# `scripts/hygiene/run.mjs` fails on an untracked test-shaped file ANYWHERE outside these,
# so this is a designated place to work, not a way to hide residue.
#
# Naming a single blessed directory did not survive contact: the hazard recurred in four
# different places, and the fourth was a lens inventing `app/zz-scratch/` rather than using
# the sanctioned path. Instruction-following at ~79% is not a mechanism. So the *-scratch
# suffix is blessed wherever it appears, which is only safe because both packages now PIN
# their vitest `include` to `test/**` — a probe in one of these can no longer join `npm test`
# whatever it is called. The ignore keeps the gate from fighting a lens mid-round; the pinned
# glob is what makes the residue harmless.
.review-scratch/
*-scratch/
*_scratch/

# tsc --build cache; regenerated on demand and machine-specific.
*.tsbuildinfo
